Yes, you can sell online courses directly or indirectly using YouTube.

How Selling Courses on YouTube Works

• Native YouTube Courses: YouTube has tested and rolled out features allowing creators to build, host, and sell courses directly on the platform so users can buy and watch content without leaving YouTube.
• External Funnels (Traditional Method): Many creators use YouTube as a top-of-funnel marketing tool. You create valuable educational videos, offer a free lead magnet (like a mini-course, masterclass, or checklist) linked in your description or pinned comments, and guide interested viewers to an email sequence or sales page on an external platform (like Teachable, Thinkific, or custom sites).
• Community and Coaching Add-ons: Modern course sales often pair video modules with community access, templates, or live coaching to deliver faster results and higher value.
Opinions on selling courses vary: some creators and viewers see it as a natural way to monetize expertise and build a business, while others feel that heavy promotional content can risk channel trust if not balanced with free value (as discussed on Reddit).
